{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039044-how-would-you-do-a-mafia-family-as-a-antagonist-in-mage","id":1039044,"title":"How would you do a mafia family as a antagonist in Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-27T12:26:35-08:00","id":1039044,"title":"How would you do a mafia family as a antagonist in Mage","content":"I was thinking up Antagonists for Mage and one idea i came up with is a Mafia family. They are not structured yet and i want advice on how to make them work in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:29:09-08:00","id":1039046,"title":"","content":"You would put your players against one of Pentacle Cabals, that's pretty much it :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:35:21-08:00","id":1039051,"title":"","content":"How <i>wouldn't</i> you do a mafia family in Mage?<br /> <br /> What kind of crime are they in? Old Family, or newcomers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:56:01-08:00","id":1039062,"title":"","content":"Seems pretty simple, it would be like the Giovanni in Modern Nights in Masquerade. Or, really, like a mafia family. Mages are the key people in charge, with proximi as their lieutenants, made men are either sleepwalkers or for whatever other reason trusted enough to do their thing.<br /> <br /> It could fit any order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T13:00:16-08:00","id":1039064,"title":"","content":"Completely agree with Vent0 here, a Mafia family taken whole cloth would work just fine in nearly any Mage or CofD Chronicle. Particularly for Mage because: <br /> <br /> 1) They're most likely going to be Sleepers so Mages will need to be extra warry about Reach and Paradox, plus unlike Supernaturals Mages can't just track Mortals since their Mage Sight can't just ping off their supernatural power usages.<br /> <br /> 2) Organized crime is clandestine in nature so the Mafia family can serve as a kind of Mystery all their own as the Troupe must investigate from the ground up who's the Godfather behind all the thugs, prostitutes, drug dealers, assassins, clueless bystandards, &quot;legitimate&quot; buisness people, and even some opportunistic Supernaturals and Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> 3) If the Mages aren't careful and it becomes apparent that operations keep getting halted by &quot;unexplainable circumstances&quot; then the Mafia Family could potentially go Hunter on the Mage Cabal and possibly the entire city. A wealthy Mafia family could theoretically make a fine Hunter Compact, and without moral compunction with the bottom line being the family buisness then every Supernatural in the city would be in danger, and super pissed at the Mages who forced their hand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 01-27-2017, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T13:14:04-08:00","id":1039069,"title":"","content":"So far i have the idea for the family's name and leadership along with a possible Supernal twist. They are called the Bertini Family and they are supposedly the oldest mafia family in the city. The leadership is comprised of old-school Sicilian gangsters and the godfather, Rocco &quot; The Hook&quot;, whose infamous for using a meat hook as a weapon. One twist i thought about them having is that they are either knowing or unknowing servitors of the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T13:14:29-08:00","id":1039070,"title":"","content":"Mafia is generally a great thing to base your mage society of. Secret world and operating in secrecy? Check. &quot;Modern feudalism&quot;? Check. Weird relationship with government/Seers? Check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T13:18:50-08:00","id":1039074,"title":"","content":"I would advice in this circumstances to structure them a little after your players and what you have in mind. I know for example that my players are pretty ruthless and don't give much for collateral damage, hence no need to play that angle.<br /> <br /> I would probably either make the mafia's intelligence really good with many officials, policemen and politicians taking their money so that they can quickly bring heat on the Mages or give them some supernatural allies or resources. Its not impossible for example that Mage enemies will happily cast spells or provide info to the mafia if the mafia can then take down the PCs, or that vampires or other creatures have built themselves a nice place inside this mafia family..<br /> <br /> You could of course always really go Giovanni style on your players and give any Moros in the cabal a day on the parade street.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T18:30:33-08:00","id":1039188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039044-how-would-you-do-a-mafia-family-as-a-antagonist-in-mage?p=1039074#post1039074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would advice in this circumstances to structure them a little after your players and what you have in mind. I know for example that my players are pretty ruthless and don't give much for collateral damage, hence no need to play that angle.<br /> <br /> I would probably either make the mafia's intelligence really good with many officials, policemen and politicians taking their money so that they can quickly bring heat on the Mages or give them some supernatural allies or resources. Its not impossible for example that Mage enemies will happily cast spells or provide info to the mafia if the mafia can then take down the PCs, or that vampires or other creatures have built themselves a nice place inside this mafia family..<br /> <br /> You could of course always really go Giovanni style on your players and give any Moros in the cabal a day on the parade street.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think of the whole being minions for a Abyssal thing? Also, i feel tempted to make on of their assassins a slasher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T18:34:57-08:00","id":1039189,"title":"","content":"Are you going for movie-like cartoonish mafia or more realistic deception of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T18:38:43-08:00","id":1039193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039044-how-would-you-do-a-mafia-family-as-a-antagonist-in-mage?p=1039189#post1039189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you going for movie-like cartoonish mafia or more realistic deception of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think i might make them mostly realistic with a bit of cartoony thrown in with a couple of members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T18:38:43-08:00","id":1039194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039044-how-would-you-do-a-mafia-family-as-a-antagonist-in-mage?p=1039189#post1039189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you going for movie-like cartoonish mafia or more realistic deception of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":".  Accidently double posted 01-27-2017, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T19:15:01-08:00","id":1039211,"title":"","content":"Watch some Sopranos, and remember: Mafia is, first and foremost, a self-help society created to pursue money. It's a business, protected by hierarchical structure and strict rules, code of honor and rule of silence and secrecy. Each member basically exists in order to provide the society with some kind of resource or services - money, expertise, strong arm or contacts. Like Consilia in Mage, they try to resolve their stuff and conflicts adhering to complicated web of written and unwritten rules of what a &quot;honorable man&quot; would do.<br /> Shooting people without a good reason is really bad for business, and shooting people from outside of Mob's world only bring in troubles; negotiate first, bribe second, break legs third, shoot fourth. And don't shoot cops. If you are having problems with cops, you fucked up should ask your higher ups for help - one of reasons why Mafia works is because they got symbiotic and good enough relationship with a lot of government officials - cops included - that with some phone calls, bribe or favor here and there, problem with get hush-hushed. <br /> Good source for Mafia drama is a situation where one of the members gets too ambitious and tries to make money on the side, without reporting (and paying the cut!) to their superiors, often against some kind of rule. Easy $$$ turn into problems, problems turn into dead bodies, Police gets involved, and you can't use your Get Out of Jail Free card because you broke the rules of Family you are probably better jailed by cops than found out by your bosses. Trapped between, such criminal would probably go to desperate measures in order to survive.<br /> So my advice would be creating such a situation, and make the troublemaker either Awaken and start doing a lot of weird shit before attempting a power grab, or approach them by Abyssal-Serving XYZ who offer help in exchange for...something, insert plot here.<br /> <br /> In general instead of fighting a monolithic mafia family, I would suggest a situation where you have &quot;noble&quot; (read: rules-abiding) main body of Mafia, &quot;The Troublemaker&quot;, Police Investigation and some sort of Abyssal Cult or entity that tries to use Troublemaker to progress their goal while hiding/saving him from both Mafia and Investigators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T20:01:14-08:00","id":1039222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039044-how-would-you-do-a-mafia-family-as-a-antagonist-in-mage?p=1039211#post1039211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watch some Sopranos, and remember: Mafia is, first and foremost, a self-help society created to pursue money. It's a business, protected by hierarchical structure and strict rules, code of honor and rule of silence and secrecy. Each member basically exists in order to provide the society with some kind of resource or services - money, expertise, strong arm or contacts. Like Consilia in Mage, they try to resolve their stuff and conflicts adhering to complicated web of written and unwritten rules of what a &quot;honorable man&quot; would do.<br /> Shooting people without a good reason is really bad for business, and shooting people from outside of Mob's world only bring in troubles; negotiate first, bribe second, break legs third, shoot fourth. And don't shoot cops. If you are having problems with cops, you fucked up should ask your higher ups for help - one of reasons why Mafia works is because they got symbiotic and good enough relationship with a lot of government officials - cops included - that with some phone calls, bribe or favor here and there, problem with get hush-hushed.<br /> Good source for Mafia drama is a situation where one of the members gets too ambitious and tries to make money on the side, without reporting (and paying the cut!) to their superiors, often against some kind of rule. Easy $$$ turn into problems, problems turn into dead bodies, Police gets involved, and you can't use your Get Out of Jail Free card because you broke the rules of Family you are probably better jailed by cops than found out by your bosses. Trapped between, such criminal would probably go to desperate measures in order to survive.<br /> So my advice would be creating such a situation, and make the troublemaker either Awaken and start doing a lot of weird shit before attempting a power grab, or approach them by Abyssal-Serving XYZ who offer help in exchange for...something, insert plot here.<br /> <br /> In general instead of fighting a monolithic mafia family, I would suggest a situation where you have &quot;noble&quot; (read: rules-abiding) main body of Mafia, &quot;The Troublemaker&quot;, Police Investigation and some sort of Abyssal Cult or entity that tries to use Troublemaker to progress their goal while hiding/saving him from both Mafia and Investigators.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI feel tempted to make the Don's son a scalesti who is trying to become don after his dad's death and turn the family into a abyss cult. Would it make since if he already has abyss cultists within the family?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T22:37:00-08:00","id":1039267,"title":"","content":"Also, something to keep in mind after this is all taken care of, if your players somehow manage to 'beat' the mafia family, sufficiently weakening them is likely to cause some sort of power vacuum in the local criminal underworld. Chances are, their actions will probably result in a spike of violent crimes as a bunch of lesser factions vie for dominance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T22:41:38-08:00","id":1039270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039044-how-would-you-do-a-mafia-family-as-a-antagonist-in-mage?p=1039188#post1039188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of the whole being minions for a Abyssal thing? Also, i feel tempted to make on of their assassins a slasher.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it sounds like fun. A Slasher enemy could give the players an enemy to fear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And like WHW said, you don't need to turn the whole gang into Abyssial servants but just a enough of them to cauise problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T04:38:12-08:00","id":1039364,"title":"","content":"Years ago ( it would be like 10 now, I think ) I run <b>Mage</b> chronicle in Venice and made one of mafia families Don an Adamant Sage on Mastigos Path. He was member of some fan created Forces/Mind Legacy from White Wolf forum ( Tytalons or something like that ). He worked PERFECTLY as Adamant Sage to Consilium - Tendancy for secrecy in Diamond Orders? Checked, in Omerta. Tendency for violent ( but not simply lethal ) resolution of conflicts? Checked, as Arrow leader. Disrespecting boundaries and public traditions, but adhering to one self? Checked, as Mastigos mage and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mafia_initiation_ritual\" target=\"_blank\">mafia rituals</a> ( some rumors says stuff as spiting on image of Holy Mary ). Really, if you need interesting and working NPC for 'Awakened mafia', you have my blessing in using this Adamant Sage concept. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T06:10:53-08:00","id":1039394,"title":"","content":"As an Italian: scrap everything about Mafia being full of &quot;honorable men&quot;. That's just a lie mafiosi tell themselves (and other people). Recently some mafiosi in Naples shot some street vendors because one didn't pay the pizzo. That's not honorable, nor smart, since, y'know, a kid got shot too. Nobody died, but it was in plain day. <i>Plain day. </i>And kids are routinely used to manifacture and sell cocaine. Even if you want a more &quot;cartoony&quot; portrayal, remember this stuff.<br /> <br /> If we are talking in Mage terms, the Mafia (<i>aka </i>Cosa Nostra, you said Sicilian, right? we have lots of different ones) are more akin to Seers. They are pervasive, they have ties to the powers that be (but aren't), they want to control the populace, even when that wouldn't be smart, just because controlling people means you have power, and having power is all that matters to the mafia, even more than money. One metaphor used to describe the organization is the octopus: there is a strict hierarchy and many arms, whose only goal is control.<br /> So, picture the Seers, power hungry, subservient, treacherous, and put a little &quot;we want more power so we'll do stupid things to have it&quot; in the equation. And yes, maybe the stupid thing is calling the Abyss for help, or perhaps some Reapers. I think Reapers are more fitting, personally. Maybe the godfather is one, and he trades in souls. If you don't pay soon enough, you get your soul &quot;stored somewhere safe&quot;. That's where the Pentacle would come in.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> PS: we don't usually use the term &quot;godfather&quot; nowadays. It's still about family, but the families are called &quot;clans&quot;. So the boss is the capoclan, aka the clan boss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":3765,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","user":"SNESferatu","date":". 01-28-2017, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T06:18:01-08:00","id":1039395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SNESferatu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1039044-how-would-you-do-a-mafia-family-as-a-antagonist-in-mage?p=1039394#post1039394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an Italian: scrap everything about Mafia being full of &quot;honorable men&quot;. That's just a lie mafiosi tell themselves (and other people). Recently some mafiosi in Naples shot some street vendors because one didn't pay the pizzo. That's not honorable, nor smart, since, y'know, a kid got shot too. Nobody died, but it was in plain day. <i>Plain day. </i>And kids are routinely used to manifacture and sell cocaine. Even if you want a more &quot;cartoony&quot; portrayal, remember this stuff.<br /> <br /> If we are talking in Mage terms, the Mafia (<i>aka </i>Cosa Nostra, you said Sicilian, right? we have lots of different ones) are more akin to Seers. They are pervasive, they have ties to the powers that be (but aren't), they want to control the populace, even when that wouldn't be smart, just because controlling people means you have power, and having power is all that matters to the mafia, even more than money. One metaphor used to describe the organization is the octopus: there is a strict hierarchy and many arms, whose only goal is control.<br /> So, picture the Seers, power hungry, subservient, treacherous, and put a little &quot;we want more power so we'll do stupid things to have it&quot; in the equation. And yes, maybe the stupid thing is calling the Abyss for help, or perhaps some Reapers. I think Reapers are more fitting, personally. Maybe the godfather is one, and he trades in souls. If you don't pay soon enough, you get your soul &quot;stored somewhere safe&quot;. That's where the Pentacle would come in.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> PS: we don't usually use the term &quot;godfather&quot; nowadays. It's still about family, but the families are called &quot;clans&quot;. So the boss is the capoclan, aka the clan boss.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNow I feel tempted to make the capoclan a willing or unwilling servant of a Tremere lich. Also, thanks for the info on the new term for godfather. And yes, they are Sicilian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T19:43:31-08:00","id":1039758,"title":"","content":"Another question. If the mobsters are actually servants of a Tremere lich how would they get Awakened souls to him or her? They would probably be unable to tell the difference between humans and Awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 01-28-2017, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T22:53:35-08:00","id":1039835,"title":"","content":"Here's my thoughts, take them for what they are worth.<br /> \u200b1-Design your mafia using the Cult merit, with advantages that fit in a 'mundane' criminal empire.<br /> \u200b2-Design a cult within the cult using a second merit tree, these are the guys in the know about the supernatural and their advantages could include such traits of their own. This is where your slasher fits in.<br /> \u200b3-Give their leadership the Fame merit as defense against sympathetic casting. Sure you and that guy you just passed on the street have never heard of them, but to the cops and other criminals they are positively famous.<br /> \u200b4-Don't start with them going head on against your players, start subtly with the two groups coming at cross purposes. Something the mafia is doing threatens the players in some way and the mafia doesn't even know the players exist, they also hide much of their activities behind 'legit' fronts. The players should already have the knife at their collective throats before they even realize there is a danger.<br /> \u200b5-Remember the octopus, the mafia is made up of many arms and the left rarely knows what the right is doing, or honestly why they themselves have been ordered to do what they are doing. In criminal empires it is common for only a few or even one person to know everything that is going on, that's why the death of one person causes so much shake up in the organization as no one else knows where all the bodies are. The players should never have the chance to read the mind of anyone who knows more than a small part until they finally go after the living heart of the family.<br /> \u200b6-If you want an abyssal angle then just come up with an abyssal shard or entity that fits what the mafia is doing, a 'rule through benign violence' sort of idea. Having only a limited part of the family falling within this group has the advantage that it will be even harder for the Mages to find someone who can give all of the secrets away, and when they finally run into someone who embodies the true horror of things it should be a horrific surprise. These guys, by the way, are the people from step '2'.<br /> \u200b7-If you go with the Tremere then the mafia doesn't collect his souls, he is the true Reaper, they are information gatherers, noisy distractions and above all canon fodder for his attack.<br /> \u200b8-Remember that when you are going up against the mafia you are not only going up against the family, but everyone else who is also chasing them. Surprise your players with the knowledge that their new tail isn't family but FBI and he wants to know their connection.<br /> \u200b9-Don't treat the mafia like a specific group of bad guys, instead they should be handled more like environmental hazards, defeating them should involve changing fundamental parts of the setting itself, changes that draw lots of unwanted attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 01-29-2017, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}